# Batch C6: Timeline / Calendar

With Global Search complete and the Content/Platform backend fully hardened, the data foundation is perfectly stable to support the Timeline module.

The goal of this batch is to provide a global birds-eye view of all scheduled and uploaded content across all clients and platforms.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> The Timeline requires deciding on a UI approach. Please review the options in the Open Questions below before we proceed.

## Open Questions

> [!WARNING]
> 1. **UI Layout Strategy:** Do you prefer a **Monthly Calendar Grid** (like Google Calendar, showing days as boxes), or a **Chronological Feed** (a vertical list grouped by Day/Week)? A chronological feed is usually better for mobile and dense content, while a grid is better for high-level planning.
> 2. **External Libraries:** If we go with a Calendar Grid, would you like me to install a library like `react-big-calendar` or `fullcalendar`? (I recommend keeping it dependency-free and building a vertical Chronological Feed for V1).
> 3. **Filtering:** I plan to add filters at the top of the Timeline for **Client**, **Platform**, and **Status**. Are there any other filters you'd find critical?

## Proposed Changes

### Backend

#### [NEW] `backend/src/controllers/timelineController.js`
- Create `getTimelineEvents(req, res)`
- Queries `Content.find({ 'platforms.scheduledDate': { $exists: true, $ne: null } })` (or uploadedDate).
- Unwinds the platforms array so each platform post acts as an individual "Event".
- Supports `?clientId=`, `?platformId=`, `?status=` query filters.
- Sorts chronologically.

#### [NEW] `backend/src/routes/timeline.js`
- Standard router for `/timeline`.

#### [MODIFY] `backend/src/server.js`
- Uncomment and mount: `app.use('/api/v1/timeline', require('./routes/timeline'));`

### Frontend

#### [MODIFY] `frontend/src/api/index.js`
- Add `timelineApi.getEvents(filters)`

#### [NEW] `frontend/src/pages/TimelinePage.jsx`
- The main hub for the timeline.
- Includes a Top Bar with Filter Dropdowns (Client, Platform, Status).
- Displays the events (either as a Grid or a Feed, pending your decision).
- Event Cards will show:
  - Scheduled Date & Time
  - Content Title & Type
  - Client Name
  - Platform Icon & Status Badge
- Clicking an event routes to `/content/:id`.

